## Private18-field handoff and source witness

Format legacy-free-admission-frontier-v1, case free-admission, exact keys:
format,source_commit,case,role,database_name,database_url,runtime_database_url,
tenant,other_tenant,namespace,run,workflow_version,scope_id,scheduler_owner,
handoff_run_version,closed_source_cutoff,producer_witness_sha256,closed_source_sha256.
Do not make inapplicable forward identity/key optional in the existing NF format.
Typed IDs/role/format/pin/DB regex/hash validation; private0700 dirs, exclusive0600
receipt.tmp, fsync+rename, no Debug/secret logs. Recorded owner free-admission-role.
The actual h=cutoff+1 is c10 entry after c9 routing. Cold current attaches ONLY the
owned admin env+validated DB name, checks receipt URLs equal derived owned URLs;
never connect through an arbitrary receipt URL. No original worker secret handoff.
Coordinator must observe old process exit before current starts; match existing
legitimate same-owner Keeper restart semantics, no lease expiry sleep or SQL edit.

PROJECTION_WITNESS_SQL unchanged proves complete pre/post migration equality.
Use common closed-scope SQL plus a new immutable free target witness (not
nonfinal_source, which requires c10 successful work/report). Bind published version,
c10 stable scope/source identity/metadata, captured items, snapshot/item payloads,
and actual original collection.entered envelope. Exclude only legitimately changing
Run/owner/scope lifecycle/stop/drain/finish/update fields. Source hash must remain
identical through native drain/finish/cold verification. Positive object/identity
checks prevent vacuous NULL witness components. Preserve complete journal prefix.

## Exact current native sequence and oracles

Full API/store bootstrap on same DB with explicit actual postgres/postgres or
sagat_app/sagat_app role proof; owner inspection is separate. Real Keeper round,
one replica, Run shard owned. Actual current frontier original scope/head,
E4200030, OPEN/no stops, next/completed0,maxConcurrency1, active empty, plain body
scope_compensates=false. No root RunTx data hydration is needed.

One advance=DrainStarted. At h+1 first root stop FAILED/RUN_DATA_LIMIT; h+2 native
c10 collection.drain_started reason run_data_limit. Exact full envelopes, root vs
owner path/id, original actor/trace, common transaction timestamp; run CANCELLING,
scope DRAINING/RDL,null iteration, exact drainUUID/seq; telemetry h+2. Exactly one
existing_outputs engine audit and one actual public FAILED drain hint with original
scope/tenant/namespace/run/trace/UUID. Everything else including counters/member/
step/checkpoint/receipt/payload/usage/closed source and old journal prefix unchanged.

Next advance=DrainFinished, not a permissive loop. Exact h+3 collection.finished detail {outcome:failed,code:RUN_DATA_LIMIT}
and h+4 run.finished detail {status:FAILED}. Scope/owner FAILED/RDL, Run FAILED,
original stop/drain intact, no result/owner output, exact finish seq/UUID and two
new collection-finished/run-finished FAILED outboxes, telemetry/journal/Run h+4.
No owner routing, admission, iteration-drained/cancel event, scoped identity, task,
saga, compensation or manual-review obligation. All four counters/reservations/
active slots remain0; payload/L/V/E and immutable source exact.

Fresh PgRunStore+DefinitionCache with scoped protocol verify_run succeeds; next
normal advance=AlreadyFinished. Full terminal state/projection identical before/
after both. Fixed safe errors (no full RunState Debug), normal Keeper leave and
five-second bounded pool closes. Handle current inspection helper's actual empty
member JSON representation explicitly. No full RunTx::data call.

